INCORPORATED SOURCES — Public Domain (NOT owned by this project)
---------------------------------------------------------------

The biblical texts, lexicons, and cross-reference apparatus this work
builds on are in the PUBLIC DOMAIN (by age or by their creators' own
dedication). The "all rights reserved" above applies ONLY to Bogdan
Zorlescu's ORIGINAL contributions — it does NOT, and cannot, restrict
these underlying public-domain sources, which anyone remains free to use
independently:

  - World English Bible (WEB) — public domain (Rainbow Missions, Inc.).
  - Strong's Hebrew & Greek lexicons (James Strong, 1890) — PD by age.
  - Treasury of Scripture Knowledge (R. A. Torrey, 1834) — PD by age.
  - Douay-Rheims, Clementine Vulgate, JPS 1917, Van Dyck Arabic,
    Westminster Leningrad Codex, Swete LXX, Byzantine Majority Text —
    public domain by age and/or their own dedication; see COPYRIGHT.md.

Per-source provenance is documented in COPYRIGHT.md and in each
`content/translations/<id>/_meta.yaml`.


